# Trainer publish

An imported profile stays `draft` until the trainer confirms the mailbox. That confirmation is the letter sent to the address they typed, or Google on the same short link. Opening `/hi/{code}` alone does not publish the card. The trainer can hide the page from the cabinet. A later confirmation does not publish a hidden or archived card.

Import, a server copy, the short-link visit, and the password step do not publish it. The confirmed mailbox does.

## Do

- Save and sync an imported profile as `draft`.
- Publish the draft when the confirmation letter is opened or Google binds the card.
- Leave the account window on the short link until the card has an owner.
- Let the trainer set the page to hidden in the cabinet.

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: the short-link visit publishes the draft
if (!staff && row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}

// right: the mailbox confirmation publishes a draft, and a hidden card stays hidden
if (row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}
```
